issue function refs on components are invoked before exposed template refs become available since 3.5.39 ### vue version 3.5.39 ### link to minimal reproduction ### steps to reproduce open the playground with vue 3.5.39 — it shows "resolved: no". switch the version to 3.5.38 — it shows "resolved: yes" ### what is expected? there should be a supported way for component function refs to access exposed template refs, for example through an exposed `nativeelement`. currently, function refs are invoked synchronously during patching, while template ref objects are assigned later in a post-render job. this means that during mount, an exposed template ref is not available yet inside the function ref and will still be `null`. ### what is actually happening? before 3.5.39, reading an exposed template ref inside a function ref caused the callback to be re-invoked after the exposed template ref was assigned because the access was tracked by the parent component's render effect. after #14985 paused tracking during function ref invocation, the callback is invoked only once, before the exposed template ref is assigned, and is never invoked again. consequently, a function ref no longer has an opportunity to access an exposed template ref. ### system info ### any additional comments? _no response_ labels issue template ref set to comment node when child component is unmounted by `v-if` ### vue version 3.5.22 ### link to minimal reproduction ### steps to reproduce 1. create a child component with `v-if` on root 2. set a template ref on the child component in the parent 3. set `v-if` condition to `false` to unmount the child root ### what is expected? template ref set to be `null` ### what is actually happening? template ref set to comment node ### system info ### any additional comments? found this while building a component using custom disclosure component. if this is not a bug, it should be documented. labels comment i don't think this is a bug. `ref="comp"` on a component points to the component public instance, and the component itself is not unmounted in this case. only its internal root branch changes from an element to the empty `v-if` branch. so `templateref.value` should remain the component instance. what changes is `templateref.value.$el`, which may point to vue's placeholder comment node when the component currently has no rendered element root. if the component itself is conditionally unmounted, e.g. ` `, then the ref should become `null`. issue fivem ### version 3.6.0-beta.17 ### reproduction link [vitejsviteacnoanhu-ue1k--5173--29a3b5f7.local-corp.webcontainer.io]( ### steps to reproduce help me fix ### what is expected? open ui ### what is actually happening? [vue warn]: unhandled error during execution of render function at at (@codem-bank/html/js/vue.global.js:1590) [vue warn]: unhandled error during execution of scheduler flush. this is likely a vue internals bug. please open an issue at . at at (@codem-bank/html/js/vue.global.js:1590) uncaught (in promise) typeerror: cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'tolocalestring') (@codem-bank/html/index.html:1106) --- fivem script codem bank v2 labels invalid can't reproduce comment its for a fivem script it just says to open an issue can anyone help comment [vue.global.js]( [vuex.global.js]( comment the reproduction link you provided shows nothing, so i'm unable to reproduce the issue. you need to submit a minimal reproducible code or repository. issue `experimental.bundleddev` fails to resolve virtual modules (breaks unocss and vue devtools) ### describe the bug when enabling the `experimental.bundleddev` option in vite, plugins that rely on injecting and serving **virtual modules** fail to work correctly. i tested this with two major ecosystem plugins: `unocss` and `vite-plugin-vue-devtools`. both broke simultaneously when `bundleddev: true` was enabled. it seems the dev server fails to resolve, bundle, or serve virtual modules, resulting in 404 errors or missing code. ##